  "type": "numeric",
  "prompt": "Calculate $\\displaystyle\\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty}\\left(\\left\\lfloor\\sqrt[n]{2010}\\right\\rfloor-1\\right)$, where $\\lfloor x\\rfloor$ is the largest integer less than or equal to $x$.",
  "image": null,
  "choices": null,
  "answer": "2077",
  "acceptedAnswers": null,
  "answerUnit": null,
  "solutions": [
   {
    "title": "Compute term by term",
    "body": "For $n\\ge11$ we have $2^{n}>2010$, so $\\sqrt[n]{2010}<2$ and the term is $1-1=0$. For $n\\le10$:\n\n| $n$ | $\\lfloor\\sqrt[n]{2010}\\rfloor$ | term |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | 2010 | 2009 |\n| 2 | 44 ($44^2=1936<2010<45^2$) | 43 |\n| 3 | 12 ($12^3=1728<2010<13^3$) | 11 |\n| 4 | 6 ($6^4=1296<2010<7^4$) | 5 |\n| 5 | 4 ($4^5=1024<2010<5^5$) | 3 |\n| 6 | 3 ($3^6=729<2010<4^6$) | 2 |\n| 7 | 2 ($3^7=2187>2010$) | 1 |\n| 8 | 2 | 1 |\n| 9 | 2 | 1 |\n| 10 | 2 ($2^{10}=1024$) | 1 |\n\nSum: $2009+43+11+5+3+2+1+1+1+1=2077$.\n\n**Answer: 2077**"
   }
  ],
