  "points": null,
  "timeMinutes": null,
  "type": "numeric",
  "prompt": "Let $f(x)=3x^3-5x^2+2x-6$. If the roots of $f$ are $\\alpha,\\beta,\\gamma$, find $$\\left(\\frac1{\\alpha-2}\\right)^2+\\left(\\frac1{\\beta-2}\\right)^2+\\left(\\frac1{\\gamma-2}\\right)^2.$$",
  "image": null,
  "choices": null,
  "answer": "68",
  "acceptedAnswers": null,
  "answerUnit": null,
  "solutions": [
   {
    "title": "Build the polynomial with roots 1/(root - 2)",
    "body": "The numbers $\\alpha-2,\\beta-2,\\gamma-2$ are the roots of $g(x)=f(x+2)=3x^3+13x^2+18x+2$. The reciprocals $y_i=\\frac1{\\alpha_i-2}$ are the roots of the reversed polynomial $h(y)=2y^3+18y^2+13y+3$.\n\nBy Vieta, $y_1+y_2+y_3=-\\frac{18}2=-9$ and $y_1y_2+y_2y_3+y_3y_1=\\frac{13}2$. Therefore\n$$\\sum y_i^2=\\Big(\\sum y_i\\Big)^2-2\\sum y_iy_j=81-13=68.$$\n\n**Answer: 68**"
   }
  ],
