  "timeMinutes": null,
  "type": "numeric",
  "prompt": "Assume that $f(a+b)=f(a)+f(b)+ab$ and that $f(75)-f(51)=1230$. Find $f(100)$.",
  "image": null,
  "choices": null,
  "answer": "3825",
  "acceptedAnswers": null,
  "answerUnit": null,
  "solutions": [
   {
    "title": "Find the general form",
    "body": "Setting $a=b=0$ gives $f(0)=0$. Taking $b=1$: $f(n+1)=f(n)+f(1)+n$, so\n$$f(n)=\\sum_{i=0}^{n-1}\\big(i+f(1)\\big)=\\frac{n(n-1)}2+nf(1).$$\nThen $f(75)-f(51)=2775-1275+24f(1)=1230$, so $24f(1)=-270$ and $f(1)=-\\frac{45}4$.\n\nFinally $f(100)=\\frac{100\\cdot99}2+100\\cdot\\left(-\\frac{45}4\\right)=4950-1125=3825$.\n\n**Answer: 3825**"
   }
  ],
